{"url": "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/support-and-financial-aid/", "final_url": "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/support-and-financial-aid/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-27", "text": "Support and Funding \u2013 Ph.D. in Ecology\nPh.D. in Ecology\nAbout\nProgram Overview\nSDSU\nUC Davis\nGive\nPeople\nContact Us\nSDSU Ecology JDP Faculty\nTeaching Associates\nDoctoral Students\nAcademics\nDegree Requirements\nMajor Areas of Study\nCourse Catalog\nResearch\nNews\nDissertation Defenses\nLabs, Centers, and Facilities\nBiodiversity Museum\nStudent Publications\nAdmissions\nAdmission Eligibility\nApplication Procedure\nFinancial Aid & Scholarships\nStudent Life\nBasic Needs Resources\nCultural Centers\nGraduate Affairs\nGraduate Housing\nStudent Disability Services\nHealth Resources\nStudent Handbook\nCost of Study and Support\nSupport and Funding\nEcology Program Forms\nStudent Handbooks\nAdvancement to Candidacy Form\nAbout\nProgram Overview\nSDSU\nUC Davis\nGive\nPeople\nContact Us\nSDSU Ecology JDP Faculty\nTeaching Associates\nDoctoral Students\nAcademics\nDegree Requirements\nMajor Areas of Study\nCourse Catalog\nResearch\nNews\nDissertation Defenses\nLabs, Centers, and Facilities\nBiodiversity Museum\nStudent Publications\nAdmissions\nAdmission Eligibility\nApplication Procedure\nFinancial Aid & Scholarships\nStudent Life\nBasic Needs Resources\nCultural Centers\nGraduate Affairs\nGraduate Housing\nStudent Disability Services\nHealth Resources\nStudent Handbook\nCost of Study and Support\nSupport and Funding\nEcology Program Forms\nStudent Handbooks\nAdvancement to Candidacy Form\nSupport and Funding\nStudents admitted to the Joint Doctoral Program Ecology (JDPE) are offered support from Graduate Research Assistantships (GAs) or Teaching Assistantships (TAs) and also receive a comprehensive benefits package. Students typically will receive support for 5 years, as long as they are making satisfactory progress and are satisfactorily discharging other responsibilities related to the stipend. The normal teaching load for students receiving these stipends is 6 hours (e.g. Two 3-hour laboratory sections) per week plus grading and preparation of assignments. Typically, students without other support TA two lab sections in their first year, none at UC Davis, and one lab section per semester in years 3-5. The current stipends vary from $31,200 to $32,700 depending on progress through the program. Additional summer RAs are often provided by individual advisors to supplement this stipend.\nFellowships, scholarships, and other forms of financial assistance from university, state, federal, and private sources are also available.\nReferences\nSDSU Financial Aid Scholarships Office\nSDSU College of Graduate Studies\nyoutube\ntwitter\nfacebook\ninstagram\n619-594-5200\n5500 Campanile Drive\nSan Diego, CA 92182\nMaps | Parking\nCampus Directory\nEmployment\nMedia Relations\nCanvas\nGeneral Contact\nNetwork Status\nStrategic Plan\nNewsletter\nAccessibility\nDocument Readers\nDigital Privacy Statement\nCampus Safety Reports\nInstitutional Disclosures\nAffirming Equal Opportunity\nFeedback\n\u00a9 2026 San Diego State University | All Rights Reserved", "links": [["", "https://www.sdsu.edu"], ["", "https://ucdavis.edu"], ["Ph.D. in Ecology", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology"], ["", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/support-and-financial-aid/#menu-main-slide"], ["Program Overview", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/program-overview/"], ["SDSU", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/sdsu/"], ["UC Davis", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/uc-davis/"], ["Give", "https://securelb.imodules.com/s/997/20/giving/form.aspx?sid=997&gid=1&pgid=3034&dids=261&bledit=1&appealcode=BIOLOGYX"], ["Contact Us", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/contact-us/"], ["SDSU Ecology JDP Faculty", "https://biology.sdsu.edu/doctoral/ecology/program-faculty/"], ["Teaching Associat